# D-MAL-01 WORLD RECORD. The ruling says Malachor V "keeps its world record - it is
# a place characters can go - but it leaves the homeworld menu." IT LEFT THE MENU
# CORRECTLY AND NEVER GOT THE RECORD. Same shape as the nine ineligible worlds and
# the two D-NOMENU-01 records: entry present, SKILL LIST EMPTY.
M["Malachor V"] = [("", [],
    "\u26a0\u26a0 NO MENU, AND THAT IS THE RULING RATHER THAN AN OMISSION. D-MAL-01: 'Sapient Species: None after D-MAL-01. NOBODY IS RAISED ON MALACHOR V. IT KEEPS ITS RECORD AS A PLACE; IT HAS NO MENU.' \u2705 THIS RECORD IS THE HALF THAT WAS MISSING. The ruling reads 'it keeps its world record - IT IS A PLACE CHARACTERS CAN GO - but it leaves the homeworld menu.' THE MENU WAS LEFT. THE RECORD WAS NEVER WRITTEN, so for the whole of this Atlas's life the world a party can travel to HAD NO ENTRY TO TRAVEL TO. \u26a0\u26a0 TORN APART IN 3960 AND EMPTY SINCE - FOUR YEARS BEFORE THE CAMPAIGN OPENS. That is not ancient history. A CHARACTER OF ANY AGE REMEMBERS IT HAPPENING. \u27e1\u27e1 PERAGUS is the sibling case and sits in the same selection: both are places rather than homeworlds and both are reachable. A GM RUNNING EITHER IS RUNNING A DESTINATION, NOT AN ORIGIN. \u2705 PLACE: the CHORLIAN SECTOR of the Outer Rim, grid S-4, selection entry 12. \u26a0 Everything the KOTOR II material attaches to this world lies after our date and is excluded as event; WHAT STANDS AT 3956 IS A BROKEN PLANET FOUR YEARS COLD.")]
